      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `installTestData` uses `android.InstallTestData` which is just a wrapper around `android.installFile`. Using `install` creates the same installation paths, but avoids a type conversion from `Path` to `DataPath`\n\nI think `nativetest64` comes from [here](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/37d4d1bd5b4356d984586376189684b948d2e702:cc/test.go;l\u003d387-388;drc\u003d90e76f1b84b8843c2b9c8ca47a809630f74aa83c;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0). Prior to this CL, the tests will be installed in a `nativetest` subdir relative to $PRODUCT_OUT in soong only mode. `InstallInTestCases` cause the \"partition\" to be evaluated as [testcases](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/37d4d1bd5b4356d984586376189684b948d2e702:android/paths.go;l\u003d2103-2106;drc\u003dd6a390014eb9b24cac72108d5619cb6bd9921e5f;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0) for both host and device.\n\nThe asymmetric installation paths between cc and python/rust is WAI imo. Running python and rust tests in soong-only mode will likely require us to install those tests in the \"testcases\" partition of the staging directory.",
      "parentUuid": "6eb0be29_29900962",
      "revId": "d65bc9537048320b41d37c0c6fc9ff2cdab5ca37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
